anat622@hotmail.com wrote:
> Boudewijn Waijers wrote:

> This reminds me of another question. I did go to the mines with a
> large cat, but it was still too low-level to attack the guard on the
> way down.  Then further down it hit a polymorph trap and turned into
> an even lower-level carnivorous ape.  I kept trying to coax it back
> into the trap, but it must've liked being an ape just fine and
> carefully avoided the trap.  Is there a trick to this?

Patience will work: a pet, however intelligent, will sometimes step on a
known trap, just as it may sometimes move onto a cursed object (the
latter only 'reluctantly'). This is not advisable, though: it might kill
you by starving. You may speed this up by surrounding the polymorph trap
by boulders, leaving one way free, and forcing your pet in the correct
direction. Still not something I'd like to do.

Better ways are standing beside the trap, and using a magic whistle
until your pet gets moved onto the trap and fails its saving throw. This
is faster than the above method, but stil not fast.

The best way works only when you have magic resistance or an amulet of
unchanging, so you may move onto the trap yourself. Stand on it, and
wait for your pet to move next to you. When it does, move towards your
pet and hope to displace it onto the trap. Repeat until it works.

